00:00:01,090 --> 00:00:13,730
Workbook, Grade 8, Book A, Unit 1, Page 123 B1.

2
00:00:13,730 --> 00:00:17,820
Kitty, David and Nora are talking about friends.

3
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:24,270
Listen to their conversation and complete the notes below.

4
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:30,330
I think friends are very important to everyone.

5
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:34,310
Yes, I think so too.

6
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:39,580
When we're sad, friends give us love and care.

7
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:44,630
When we're happy, we can share our joy with them.

8
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:46,700
Yes, I agree.

9
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:51,930
If we don't have any friends, we may feel very lonely.

10
00:00:51,930 --> 00:00:56,710
I also think a friend in need is a friend indeed.

11
00:00:56,710 --> 00:01:02,400
A true friend will help us when things are difficult. That's right.

12
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:06,590
We should always be ready to help our friends.

13
00:01:06,590 --> 00:01:12,720
And we should thank our friends when they help us. True.

14
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:17,990
We should make as many friends as we can.

15
00:01:17,990 --> 00:01:22,330
Having more friends can make us happier.

16
00:01:22,330 --> 00:01:28,550
Yes, and friends should always be kind, honest and helpful.

17
00:01:28,550 --> 00:01:33,180
I believe that good friends will help us be like that too.
